 "title": "Тебе нужнее  (You Need It More)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "max": "Макс",
  "passerby": "Прохожий"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Left alone outside after his fight with Vika, Max turns to a stranger, and then hands something over. Here it is in Russian.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Извините. Это нормально, да?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "passerby",
   "t": "Ну, бывает.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На, держись, старик.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Тебе нужнее.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now the words up close.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Извините. Это нормально, да?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Excuse me. Is this normal?' Russian uses \"normalno\", 'normal', all the time for 'okay' or 'fine'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "passerby",
   "t": "Ну, бывает.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, it happens.' The word \"byvaet\", 'it happens', is what you say in Russian to shrug something off.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На, держись, старик.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here. Hang in there, old man.' Russian hands things over with \"na\", a little word like 'here, take it', and \"derzhis\" literally means 'hold on'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Тебе нужнее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You need it more.' The word \"nuzhnee\" means 'more needed', so \"tebe nuzhnee\" is literally 'to you it's more needed'. Here's the street scene again.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Извините. Это нормально, да?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "passerby",
   "t": "Ну, бывает.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На, держись, старик.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Тебе нужнее.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max gives it away and walks on. Russians say \"starik\", 'old man', to an old man, but also to a close friend of any age. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Пока!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
